        "id": "GO:0015221",
        "isObsolete": false,
        "name": "lipopolysaccharide transmembrane transporter activity",
        "definition": {
          "text": "Enables the transfer of lipopolysaccharides from one side of a membrane to the other. A lipopolysaccharide is any of a group of related, structurally complex components of the outer membrane of Gram-negative bacteria. Lipopolysaccharides consist three covalently linked regions, lipid A, core oligosaccharide, and an O side chain. Lipid A is responsible for the toxicity of the lipopolysaccharide.",
